   793 				;=============================================================================
   794 				; Selector status line (row 20) - the highlighted image's original long source
   795 				; filename.  It is not on the Atari disk (8.3 short names only); it lives in the
   796 				; image's .NFO as record 1, the "Input                : <name>" line.  Reading a
   797 				; whole .NFO per row stuttered a fresh directory, so instead the converter
   798 				; writes all the names once into "IMAGES.LST" (8-byte key + name per record)
   799 				; beside the images.  Nfo_Name_LoadManifest slurps that in one pass on every
   800 				; Rescan_Images into NFO_NAME_VRAM (NFO_NAME_SLOT bytes/ordinal); the draw path
   801 				; is then a pure VRAM read.  No IMAGES.LST -> every slot stays $00 -> the line
   802 				; is simply blank.
   803 				;=============================================================================
   804
